  "body": "## What changed\n\nThis PR is the app part of #3646. It builds on the #4201 component commands. It does not depend on PR #4233, and it does not touch `crates/app/src/project/`.\n\n- `DocumentComponent` (`crates/app/src/schema.rs`) has two new fields:\n  - `milling: Option<MillingBody>`: the catalog facts of a multi-seat cutter body. Only a tool item can have them.\n  - `running: Option<InsertRunning>`: the tool material and the cutting rows of an insert. Only an insert can have them.\n- `tool_assembly::derive`: when the insert sits on a body row with cutter facts, the tool gets the whole milling record from the #4192 resolver (`milling_cutter::derive(..).assembled(..)`). This includes the kind, the diameter, the corner, the flutes, the flute length, centre cutting and the enclosed holder. The resolver checks every seat. The running data of the insert goes on each tool that cuts with that insert. This includes the single-seat insert path.\n- `UpsertDocumentComponent::with_row` and `EditDocumentComponent::with_row` take the whole row. `EditDocumentComponent::new` keeps the facts and the running data of the held row. The command refuses a fact on the wrong kind of component when the row is made. It also refuses running rows that a milling tool cannot take.\n- An edit of the shared insert updates each tool that uses it in one undo step. The operations go Stale through their stamps, as in #3644.\n- Decision: `docs/decisions/3646-multi-seat-record.md`.\n\n## Pinning tests\n\nNew submodule `crates/app/tests/tool_library_holders/multi_seat.rs`, in the existing `tool_library_holders` binary (no new top-level binary):\n- `a_multi_seat_cutter_takes_its_whole_record_from_the_document`: a 4-seat Ø50 face mill and a 2-seat Ø25 end mill with one shared insert. Each tool gets the flutes, the flute length, centre cutting, the tool material and the cutting rows.\n- `a_shared_insert_edit_updates_both_multi_seat_tools_in_one_undo_step`: the corner and the cutting rows change on the two tools, the two operations go Stale, and undo and redo restore the exact state.\n- `an_edit_that_breaks_a_seat_is_refused_by_the_tool_name`: a D insert in the S seats, and `DC` away from the seats, are refused. The refusal names the component and the tool, and nothing changes.\n- `the_face_mill_is_refused_a_plunge_into_solid`: the face mill (not centre-cutting) gets `CENTER_CUT_REFUSAL` on a tight Bore. The centre-cutting end mill bores its hole.\n\n## Gate results (head 3ab6f4ae3)\n\n- Pinning tests: `cargo xtask gate test multi_seat --crate camcraft-app --binary tool_library_holders`: 4 passed.\n- Quick gate: `cargo xtask gate quick --base origin/main`: 42 steps, 0 failed. This includes `app suites: tool_library_holders` and `ui suites: machine`.\n- Clippy: `cargo clippy -p camcraft-app --all-targets -- -D warnings`: clean.\n- Light lane: `cargo xtask gate light`: 6 steps, 0 failed.\n- Heavy step: none (P6).\n- Example catalog suites: not run. No post or toolpath generator changed.\n\n## Not exercised\n\n- The project file does not keep the table yet (#3645, PR #4233). The two new fields must go into that format when the two PRs meet.\n- When the two PRs meet, these files get small text conflicts: `schema.rs` (each PR adds a field) and `commands/tool_assembly.rs` (the row literals; each PR adds `with_row`). Keep both sides.\n- There is no MCP tool for the new constructors. #3647 owns the component MCP tools.\n\n## What remains on #3646\n\n- The project-file format for `milling` and `running`, after #4233.\n- A holder collision test on an operation with an indexable face mill. The envelope is pinned in `camcraft-tools` (#4192), and this PR asserts the enclosed holder on the record.\n\nChangelog: Multi-seat indexable face mills and end mills take their whole tool record (flutes, flute length, centre cutting, tool material, cutting rows) from the document's tool components; one edit of the shared insert updates every such tool in one undo step.\n\nEffort: high\n\nRefs #3646\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
